      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "The **Guarded Write Journal** page describes how the guarded write path journals prior file state for rollback on failure. Specifically:\n\nAccording to [[write-journal]], before any file is overwritten, the system first records its prior state \u2014 either its previous content (if it existed) or a record that it did not exist \u2014 into an in-memory write journal. If the agent run later fails (due to exceeding a turn cap, an unrecoverable error, or write denials), the journal can roll back every recorded write in reverse order: restoring previous content for existing files and deleting newly created files.\n\nThis approach provides **all-or-nothing semantics** for writes without requiring a database transaction \u2014 the in-memory journal itself serves as the transaction log for the duration of a single run.\n\nThe article also notes that the Query agent doesn\u0027t use the journal\u0027s rollback capabilities since it has no write tool, though the journal type exists in the shared agent runtime library.",
      "input_tokens": 5442,
      "output_tokens": 211
    }
